export const AE_DOCS: Record<string, AeDoc> = {
  "ae-conventions": {"title":"After Effects conventions — units, time, alpha, color","body":"What a toolbox value becomes in After Effects. All of it is already done\nfor you by the exporter (`src/lib/ae-export/convert/`); read this to\nexplain a mismatch, not to redo the math. Numbers marked *measured* were\nread back from AE 26.5 (spec 091926_after-effects-handoff.md §13).\n\n## Space\n\n- Toolbox authors in canvas01: Y-down, width-relative. AE is Y-down\n  pixels. `x_px = x·W`, `y_px = H/2 + (y − 0.5)·W`. Exact.\n- Width-relative radii and stroke widths are `·W` px on both axes. Stroke\n  `px` units pass through; `%` is `·W/100`.\n- `uv01` / `v_uv` (Gradient, GLSL) is **Y-up**: `(x, 1 − y_raster)`. The\n  one inversion to watch.\n- Angles on the layer transform are degrees, clockwise on a Y-down screen.\n  Toolbox `sample-along-path` angles and `copy-to-points` rotations are\n  radians.\n\n## Transforms\n\n- A Transform node is an AE layer transform: `anchorPoint = pivot_px`,\n  `position = pivot_px + translate_px`, `scale = [sx, sy]·100`,\n  `rotation = degrees`. Same operation order as toolbox, so non-uniform\n  scale under rotation matches.\n- `space=local` pivots resolve against the geometry's bounding box. If that\n  box animates, the anchor is keyed per frame.\n- Gizmos become null layers; a wired transform chain becomes `layer.parent`.\n- AE's Scale is a 3-D property even on a 2-D layer (*measured*); the\n  builder pads eases and values.\n- Independent X / Y tracks export as separated dimensions.\n\n## Time\n\n- Toolbox time is integer ticks, 1000 per frame. AE keys are seconds:\n  `t = tick / 1000 / fps`.\n- Keys are written in the containing comp's time, even on a layer with a\n  non-zero `startTime` (*measured*).\n- Layer clip windows become `inPoint` / `outPoint`; the layer-local clock\n  offset becomes `startTime`. Windows on one clock emit straight into the\n  main comp; windows on different clocks become one precomp, placed once\n  per window with that window's start time.\n- The Toolbox Shader effect's clock is layer time × Time Speed + Time\n  Offset (equal to comp time for layers that start at 0).\n\n## Easing\n\n- **Editable** (default): one AE segment per toolbox segment. Exact for\n  linear, quad, cubic, back (exact cubics), hold, `customBezier` and\n  `cubicBezier`. Best-fit cubics elsewhere: in-out quad 0.30%, in-out\n  cubic 0.26%, sine ≤ 0.008%, expo 0.0975% (a floor: `easeOf` jumps by\n  2⁻¹⁰ next to the key).\n- **Exact**: adds keys — midpoint keys make in-out quad/cubic exact;\n  elastic drops to 0.049% with 10 keys.\n- Bounce is exact as 5 keys; elastic is 8 keys (0.117%) under Editable.\n- Springs become per-frame keys, exact at frames only.\n- AE's minimum influence is 0.1%: a `cubicBezier` handle sitting on its key\n  costs ~3e-4.\n- Position, color and path keys have one ease for all dimensions, and AE\n  never plays them past their keys: a negative speed is stored as 0 and an\n  over-long handle is shortened (*measured*). Back and elastic on those\n  become per-frame keys. Per-dimension eases overshoot freely.\n\n## Color\n\n- Toolbox interpolates keyed colors in **OKLab** (default) or RGB; AE always\n  interpolates RGB. A red→blue tween differs badly at the midpoint.\n- Policy `auto` (default): an OKLab-lerp **expression** on shape / solid\n  colors (exact; it sits on the track's own keys, which stay editable),\n  **dense keys** within 2/255 elsewhere (red→blue 63 keys, orange→teal 56,\n  black→white 9). `rgb` accepts AE's interpolation and reports the worst\n  ΔE; a segment AE can't play within tolerance (an in-out cubic, whose fit\n  dips below 0) still goes dense.\n- AE solids can't key their color, so a keyed solid color becomes a\n  comp-sized rectangle shape layer.\n- One-ease color speed is in 0–255 units per second (*measured*).\n- An 8-digit hex color's alpha rides a separate opacity track.\n- Ramps are sampled into gradient stops within 1/255; `srgb` ramps map 1:1.\n- The builder sets the project's color settings explicitly (bit depth,\n  sRGB working space, linear blending off) and the report says which.\n\n## Alpha\n\n- Toolbox composites straight alpha. AE hands effects **straight** pixels\n  and expects straight ones back (*measured*); its compositing is\n  premultiplied internally, so anti-aliased edges of blended layers can\n  differ by a sub-pixel amount.\n- aerender's \"TIFF Sequence with Alpha\" writes **premultiplied** pixels.\n  Unpremultiply before comparing with toolbox frames.\n\n## Effects, masks, mattes\n\n- Effect params are addressed as `<match>-<4-digit param ID>`: the ID, not\n  the param's position in Effect Controls, for built-ins\n  (`ADBE Gaussian Blur 2-0001`) and third-party effects alike\n  (`TBX Shader-0020`) (*measured*).\n- AE hands a shape or text layer's effects a buffer cropped to its content;\n  toolbox filters frame-sized images. Effects therefore go on a comp-sized\n  precomp of the layer.\n- Echo and Displacement Map read their layer's source frames and ignore\n  effects earlier on the layer, so their inputs are precomposed.\n- Some nodes are two AE effects on one layer (Posterize = Levels, then\n  Posterize; Threshold = a Channel Mixer, then Threshold). The per-node docs\n  (`ae-nodes/<type>`) give each map and its measured error.\n- A layer param (`PF_Param_LAYER`) is set by layer index; AE then follows\n  the layer, not the index.\n- Merge's per-layer matte is a track matte set by reference\n  (`setTrackMatte`, AE 23+): Luma when the mask is an image (luma × alpha),\n  Alpha when it's a spline; `maskInvert` gives the Inverted type.\n- The universal `mask` input: a spline mask on an AE effect becomes that\n  effect's Compositing Options mask, on one layer. An image mask makes the\n  effected layer, luma-matted, over an un-effected copy — exact by\n  construction.\n- An effect's Compositing Options mask follows the mask's mode: Add = effect\n  inside, Subtract = outside, **None is ignored**, and a referenced mask\n  stops masking the layer (*measured*). Effect-only masks are mode Add.\n- 24 of toolbox's 29 blend modes exist in AE. Average, Negation, Reflect,\n  Glow and Phoenix don't: those regions become shader regions or bakes.\n\n## Gradients\n\n- AE scripting can't set gradient stop colors directly. The route depends\n  on the gradient's structure; both are verified in AE 26.5:\n  - **SVG seed** (default): gradient groups at the top of a shape layer,\n    holding only static paths with flat or gradient fills and plain\n    strokes, move into an SVG imported as cropped shape layers: native,\n    editable Gradient Fills. The rest of the layer stays native underneath.\n    Works headless and in the app.\n  - **`.ffx` preset**: gradients in composed contents (modifiers, group\n    transforms, keys, dashes). A synthesized preset is applied to the\n    gradient's Colors; stops land within 2/255 (*measured*). Needs the AE\n    app build: aerender hangs on `applyPreset`, so a headless build shows\n    AE's default gradient and the report says so.\n- A Gradient node (2-stop linear or radial) is Gradient Ramp on a solid.\n- Animated gradient stops can't be scripted at all: shader region or bake.\n\n## Text\n\n- Text becomes an AE text layer. Fonts are PostScript names and must be\n  installed on the AE machine; the report lists them.\n- New text layers inherit AE's Character panel settings, so the builder\n  sets every attribute explicitly.\n- Glyph metrics differ between toolbox's rasterizer and AE, so text is\n  `approx`.\n- Text animators, text on a path, keyed text documents and gradient or\n  image fills bake for now.\n\n## Instances\n\n- Copy to Points copies are evaluated as toolbox draws them, then exported\n  in one of two forms:\n  - **Repeaters**: static copies on a regular lattice, identical but for\n    position, of one plain shape instance;\n  - **exploded**: one precomp per variant, one layer per copy, up to the\n    layer budget (default 200).\n- Copy layers stack variant-major, then by `draw_order`, as toolbox packs\n  them.\n- Per copy: position, rotation, scale and opacity on the layer transform.\n  `tint_attr` becomes a Fill effect (flat instance) or a Channel Mixer.\n- A Repeater carries an opacity ramp only when it is exactly linear along\n  each axis (opacities multiply across nested Repeaters). AE's Repeater\n  Scale compounds per copy, so a per-copy scale always explodes.\n- Animated copies are keyed every frame with linear stretches merged.\n  Keyed `scale_mul_default` / `rotate_add_default` keep their eases. A pick\n  that changes over time uses HOLD opacity per variant.\n- These bake: a changing point count, a draw order that changes over time,\n  animated image fields, and points computed from an image upstream.\n- Static image fields are sampled at export from the editor's readback.\n- Array in spline mode becomes Repeaters; toolbox has no radial array.\n\n## ExtendScript\n\n- AE 26.5's ExtendScript reads `a ? x : b ? y : z` as\n  `(a ? x : b) ? y : z` (*measured*). Never nest ternaries in `.jsx`.\n"},
  "ae-host": {"title":"The Toolbox Shader plug-in and shader bundles","body":"How a fused GLSL Expression runs inside After Effects. The AE user\ninstalls one plug-in, **Toolbox Shader** (match name `TBX Shader`, in the\nEffect ▸ AE Plugins menu); every shader region ships as a bundle it loads.\nSource: `../AE_Plugins/toolbox-shader` (C++ / Metal, Mac only for now).\n\n## The bundle (`shaders/<id>.tbxfx`)\n\n- JSON of `AeShaderBundle` (`src/lib/ae-export/types.ts`): the fused GLSL\n  (kept for traceability), its Metal translation (`source.msl`), the\n  params with their pool slots, LUTs, the image inputs used, fps,\n  loopFrames, the canvas it was proven on, and `hostMin`.\n- `id` is a stable 24-bit hash of the bundle; it is the value of the\n  effect's Bundle ID param.\n- The plug-in loads `shaders/<id>.tbxfx` next to the saved `.aep` (or from\n  `~/Library/Application Support/Toolbox Shader/bundles/`). After the\n  project is saved once with the file present, the bundle lives inside the\n  `.aep` and the file is no longer needed.\n- A bundle whose `hostMin` is newer than the installed plug-in renders\n  transparent with \"Update Toolbox Shader (needs x.y.z)\".\n\n## Params\n\n| Disk ID | Param |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Bundle ID |\n| 2 | Time Speed (multiplier, default 1; 0 makes Time Offset the whole clock) |\n| 3 | Time Offset |\n| 4 | Loop Frames |\n| 10–13 | Layer A–D (image inputs `u_a`..`u_d`) |\n| 20–51 | Sliders 1–32 (scalar channels) |\n| 60–67 | Colors 1–8 (color channels, straight RGBA) |\n| 70–77 | Points 1–8 (reserved) |\n| 80–87 | Checkboxes 1–8 (toggle channels) |\n\n- Scripts address params by match name, `TBX Shader-<4-digit disk ID>`,\n  never by display name: the plug-in hides unused slots and renames used\n  ones after the bundle's channels.\n- Set **Bundle ID first** (changing it resets the other controls), then\n  only the bundle's own controls (hidden ones refuse `setValue`).\n- The project must be saved before Bundle ID is set, or the plug-in has no\n  folder to find `shaders/` in (aerender can use `TBX_SHADER_BUNDLES`).\n\n## Channel → param\n\n- scalar → slider; toggle → checkbox; color → color.\n- enum (`pick()`) → baked: the current option becomes a constant. Port only\n  the selected branch.\n- ramp / curve → a LUT texture (at most 8) sampled from the channel's\n  current value. An **animated** ramp can't be a LUT: that region bakes.\n- More than 32 scalars, 8 colors or 8 LUTs is refused.\n\n## Translation (fused GLSL → Metal)\n\nDone by `glslToMsl` (`src/lib/ae-export/shader/`) and checked by\n`validate_ae_shader` before anything reaches AE. It refuses, with the GLSL\nline:\n\n- `dFdx` / `dFdy` / `fwidth`;\n- preprocessor use other than `#version 300 es` and constant `#define`s;\n- `texture()` with a bias, `texelFetch` / `textureSize` with a LOD other\n  than literal 0, textureProj / Offset / Grad, pack / unpack;\n- a swizzle or vector component passed as an `out` argument;\n- `discard` inside helpers (in `main()` it returns transparent);\n- uniform arrays, non-2D samplers, local structs, `gl_*` other than\n  `gl_FragCoord`;\n- `==` on matrices, structs or arrays.\n\nRewrite around a refusal in the GLSL node itself, re-run `get_shader_errors`\nand `compare_renders`, then validate again.\n\n## Conventions inside the plug-in\n\n- `v_uv` is Y-up over the layer; `u_res` is the output size at the current\n  downsample; `u_aspect = W / H`; `u_frame = u_time × fps`.\n- Inputs arrive straight (unpremultiplied); the shader returns straight\n  RGBA; nothing is premultiplied on either side.\n- Out-of-range `texelFetch` clamps to the edge (WebGL2 returns 0).\n- LUTs are float in the plug-in and RGBA16F in toolbox: up to ~5e-4 apart.\n- Bundles compile with Metal's **fast math**, as toolbox's WebGL does\n  (ANGLE on Metal), so hash noise like `fract(sin(x)·43758.5…)` matches;\n  the plug-in keeps a NaN / infinity guard fast math can't remove.\n- 8, 16 and 32 bpc all work; 32 bpc keeps over-range values.\n- A shader that fails to compile renders transparent and the effect's\n  status line shows \"Compile error: msl <line>:<col>: …\".\n\n## Tools on the plug-in's side\n\n- `tbxshader-check file.tbxfx [--json]` compiles a bundle exactly as the\n  plug-in will (exit 0 = compiles).\n- `tbxshader-render file.tbxfx --size WxH --time t [--a in.png] [--set slider3=0.5] -o out.png`\n  renders a bundle offline — the reference for parity checks.\n"},
  "ae-parity": {"title":"Reading After Effects parity diffs","body":"`compare_ae_renders` renders the built `.aep` with aerender at the plan's\nframes and compares each with toolbox's own render at the same tick:\n`A | B | heat` grid plus metrics, the same oracle as `compare_renders`.\nNumbers first, diff shape second, the picture last.\n\n## Fix the highest-ranked cause first\n\n1. **A unit mismatch** — the diff is everywhere, shaped like the content\n   (blur too soft or too sharp, a stroke too thick, a shape the wrong\n   size). Usually an effect param's unit map (blur radius ↔ Blurriness),\n   a `%` stroke width, or a width-relative radius. A param edit.\n2. **A premultiplication fringe** — dark or light halos only on\n   anti-aliased edges. aerender's TIFF output is premultiplied; the\n   compare must unpremultiply. If it already does, it's a reader or\n   plug-in bug: report it, don't edit the shader.\n3. **A Y flip** — the shader region is mirrored top↔bottom. `v_uv` is\n   Y-up in both places; a flip is a plug-in bug: report it.\n4. **A gamma / working-space shift** — a uniform brightness or saturation\n   offset across the whole frame, worst in midtones. Check the project's\n   bit depth, working space and linear blending against what the report\n   says the builder set.\n5. **Color interpolation** — differences only mid-tween on keyed colors.\n   That's OKLab vs RGB: switch that track's color policy to expression or\n   dense keys.\n6. **Easing shape** — position or value off mid-segment, exact on the\n   keys. Editable fits are within 0.3%; use the Exact policy.\n7. **Hash noise** — speckled differences in noise built from\n   `fract(sin(x)·43758.5…)`. Both sides compile with fast math, so this\n   should be near zero; if it isn't, check the installed plug-in is the\n   fast-math build (`tbxshader-check --json` reports its version).\n8. **LUT precision / edge fetches** — ≤ ~5e-4 on ramp channels, or a\n   one-pixel border difference from `texelFetch` clamping.\n9. **Text** — glyph positions shift with the font AE has installed. Text is\n   `approx`; offer outlines when it must match.\n10. **Blend modes at 8 / 16 bpc** — soft-light variants and clamping;\n    32 bpc removes the clamping.\n\n## Stop rules\n\n- Stop on a match, after 4 rounds, or when a round doesn't improve any\n  frame — and say which.\n- Never call a bake a port: baked footage keeps the look and loses\n  editability.\n- Report approximations with the metric they settled at.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/array": {"title":"Array → Repeaters (spline / point) or Motion Tile (image)","type":"array","class":"instances","body":"- **Spline mode** becomes Repeaters on the fill's / stroke's shape layer.\n  - The instance path sits in a group whose transform is the per-copy TRS:\n    anchor = the canvas centre, position = the first cell's centre + Copy\n    X / Y, rotation = Copy Rotate, scale = Copy Scale × 100.\n  - One Repeater per axis: `flow-rows` steps X inside, `flow-columns` Y\n    inside. Steps are `1/count` (fit) or Cell W / H (step), × W px.\n  - Exact. Keyed or wired array params fall back to the evaluated copies\n    (path keys per frame).\n- **Point mode** outputs a lattice of points. Copy to Points maps a lattice\n  to Repeaters on its instance's shape layer, the array's per-copy rotation\n  and scale included.\n- **Image mode** maps to **Motion Tile** (`ADBE Tile`).\n  - Tile Width = 100 / countX %, Tile Height = 100 / countY % (or 100 ·\n    sizeW / sizeH in step mode).\n  - Tile Center is the centre of toolbox's bottom-left tile; Motion Tile\n    repeats from any tile.\n  - Output 100%, no mirror edges.\n  - Measured: mean ≤ 0.013 (resampling: toolbox samples without mipmaps);\n    2×2 is exact.\n  - **Falls back** (exploded layers or shader) when:\n    - a step grid doesn't cover the frame (toolbox leaves the rest\n      transparent, Motion Tile tiles on);\n    - there are pattern offsets, per-copy offsets, rotation or scale;\n    - a modulator input is wired.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/bevel-emboss": {"title":"Bevel / Emboss → shader","type":"bevel-emboss","class":"shader","body":"- Not Bevel Alpha: AE's Bevel Alpha is one light shading the alpha edge.\n  Toolbox's bevel is a JFA distance field with two lights and four styles.\n- Measured on a transparent disc (outer bevel, every light angle): mean 0.21.\n- Exports as a Toolbox Shader region (9-tap gather).\n"},
  "ae-nodes/bloom": {"title":"Bloom → Glow (look match)","type":"bloom","class":"effect","body":"- Maps to **Glow** (`ADBE Glo2`), based on Color Channels.\n  - Glow Threshold = 255 · threshold.\n  - Glow Radius = 2^(levels + 1) px.\n  - Glow Intensity = 3 · intensity.\n- Approximate, a look match: toolbox's mip pyramid, max-channel soft knee\n  and unclamped add are not Glow's blur.\n  - Measured on a bright disc and dots over dim noise: mean 0.007–0.028,\n    p95 up to 0.17 (levels 5 at intensity 2).\n  - Toolbox can exceed 1; at 8 / 16 bpc both clamp.\n- **Falls back to shader** for tint_amount > 0 and for anamorphic.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/blur": {"title":"Blur → Gaussian Blur (calibrated)","type":"blur","class":"effect","body":"- Maps to **Gaussian Blur** (`ADBE Gaussian Blur 2`): Blur Dimensions\n  horizontal and vertical, Repeat Edge Pixels on.\n- **Blurriness = 1.7464 · radius.** AE's kernel is σ = Blurriness / 3.50 in\n  linear light and toolbox's is σ = radius / 2 (R² 0.999999996, radius 2–42).\n  A keyed radius converts key by key.\n- AE 26.5's Gaussian Blur always blurs in **linear light**: it decodes with a\n  pure 2.404 power, convolves, and re-encodes. It stands in for toolbox's\n  default `linearize: on`; `linearize: off` (gamma space) has no AE twin.\n- Measured on a disc, a 1-px grid, noise and a transparent disc (radius\n  1–42, 8 and 16 bpc): mean ≤ 0.033, p95 ≤ 0.051.\n  - The worst case is the 1-px grid. Toolbox decodes piecewise sRGB, AE a\n    pure power, so mixed fine detail sits up to 0.033 brighter in AE.\n  - Noise and soft content: ≤ 0.002 mean.\n  - Alpha matches: both blur premultiplied.\n- **Falls back to shader** for:\n  - mode bokeh or convolve;\n  - `linearize: off`;\n  - radius above 42.67, toolbox's 64-tap cap (AE's kernel keeps growing).\n- Never in a linearized working space: Gaussian Blur 2 then linearizes twice\n  (γ ≈ 5.4). The builder keeps `linearizeWorkingSpace` off.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/chromatic-aberration": {"title":"Chromatic Aberration → shader","type":"chromatic-aberration","class":"shader","body":"- AE has no flat-image chromatic aberration.\n  - VR Chromatic Aberrations (`Mettle SkyBox Chromatic Aberrat`) is a 360°\n    effect for equirectangular frames: field of view, frame layout, a point\n    of interest on the sphere.\n  - It is not toolbox's radial / directional channel offset (measured mean\n    0.019 at its defaults, p95 0.094).\n- Exports as a Toolbox Shader region (3-tap gather).\n"},
  "ae-nodes/color-correction": {"title":"Color Correction → Brightness & Contrast + Hue/Saturation","type":"color-correction","class":"effect","body":"- Two effects, in toolbox's order:\n  1. **Brightness & Contrast**, Use Legacy on.\n     - Brightness = 255 · b.\n     - Contrast = 100 · (1 − 1/k) for k ≥ 1, 100 · (k − 1) below. Legacy\n       contrast scales about 0.5 by 1/(1 − c/100) or 1 + c/100.\n  2. **Hue/Saturation**: Master Hue = hue °.\n- Measured: mean ≤ 0.009 (hue, brightness + contrast, all three together).\n- **Falls back to shader** for:\n  - saturation ≠ 1 (toolbox scales HSV saturation, AE's Master Saturation is\n    HSL-based; measured off);\n  - the lift / gamma / gain / offset wheels, temp / tint, pivot ≠ 0.5,\n    midtone detail, black offset;\n  - the RGB curves (Curves is CUSTOM_VALUE: not scriptable).\n"},
  "ae-nodes/copy-to-points": {"title":"Copy to Points → Repeaters or one layer per copy","type":"copy-to-points","class":"instances","body":"The exporter evaluates every copy the way the node draws it (the point ×\nthe modulation, the tint and opacity attributes, the variant pick, the draw\norder) and then picks a form.\n\n- **Repeaters** (one shape layer, editable) when all of these hold:\n  - the copies are static and sit on a lattice: a Grid, an Array in point\n    mode, or any points that step regularly, row- or column-major, along\n    any two step vectors (a tilted lattice works);\n  - every copy has the same rotation and scale, and there is one variant\n    and no tint;\n  - the instance renders as one plain shape layer.\n\n  The copy transform (point rotation / scale × `scale_mul` /\n  `rotate_add`) becomes the instance group's transform, with one Repeater\n  per axis, fast axis inside and later copies on top. An opacity that is\n  exactly linear along each axis (`inner(col) · outer(row)`) rides the\n  Repeaters' Start / End Opacity. AE's Repeater Scale compounds per copy\n  about a fixed point, so a per-copy scale is never a Repeater.\n- **Exploded** otherwise. Each variant collapses into one precomp, and each\n  copy is one layer of it:\n  - anchor = the variant's anchor. For an image instance, `custom` is a\n    fraction of the instance image; `content center` uses the spline's\n    bounds, which is approx (toolbox reads alpha bounds at ≤ 128 px).\n  - position = the point;\n  - rotation / scale = the point's × the modulation;\n  - opacity = `opacity_attr` × 100;\n  - `tint_attr`: a **Fill** effect (its colour × the tint) on a\n    flat-coloured instance, else a **Channel Mixer** (R-R / G-G / B-B =\n    100 · tint).\n- **Stacking** is toolbox's order: variant-major (all of variant 1, then\n  2…), then `draw_order` (points order, by y, shuffled).\n- **Variants** come from a Combine (`collect`) in image mode, one precomp\n  per item. Every pick mode is replayed with the node's own code: all,\n  random, cycle, by index, target group, attribute, and image with a static\n  pick field. Another image group as the instance bakes.\n- The **layer budget** (default 200) counts copy layers. Past it the node\n  bakes; \"Keep procedural\" explodes anyway, with a warning.\n- **Time**:\n  - keyed `scale_mul_default` / `rotate_add_default` over static points →\n    each copy's Scale / Rotation keys, converted from the track (the\n    authored eases);\n  - anything else animated (the points, Stagger phases, a timed Point\n    Expression, wired modulation, attributes) → each copy's values at every\n    frame, with linear stretches merged (exact at frames);\n  - a pick that changes over time → one layer per variant a point uses,\n    shown by HOLD opacity keys;\n  - a point count or draw order that changes over time **bakes**, because\n    AE can't reorder layers over time.\n- **Fields**: a static `scale_field` / `rotate_field` / image pick is\n  sampled per copy at export from the editor's readback\n  (`AeSceneOptions.fieldPixels`). Image mode uses the shader's bilinear R\n  sample; spline mode runs the node's own compute on that readback. An\n  animated field, or no readback, bakes. `driver_field` does nothing in\n  image mode; in spline mode it bakes.\n- Points computed from an image upstream bake, because the walk's evaluator\n  has no pixels. Examples: Scatter density, Set Named Attribute from an\n  image.\n- Spline mode copies are paths: Repeaters on the same lattice rule, else\n  the evaluated geometry.\n- Point rotation fields are radians in toolbox; AE gets degrees. Toolbox\n  has no radial point generator.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/displace": {"title":"Displace → Displacement Map","type":"displace","class":"effect","body":"- Maps to **Displacement Map** (`ADBE Displacement Map`).\n  - The `displacement` input becomes a hidden layer the effect references.\n  - Map Behavior: Stretch Map to Fit; Wrap off; Expand Output off.\n- Units:\n  - Max Horizontal Displacement = amountX · W / 2 px.\n  - Max Vertical Displacement = −amountY · H / 2 px (toolbox's Y is up).\n  - Use For: r → Red, g → Green, b → Blue, a → Alpha, luminance → Luminance.\n- Measured: mean ≤ 0.008; the luminance channel's worst is 0.10, since AE's\n  luminance weights differ.\n- Edge: AE leaves pixels pushed past the frame transparent. Toolbox's\n  default `clamp` repeats the edge instead, so an alpha band appears there\n  (α mean 0.016 at amount 0.05, 0.06 at 0.2). `transparent` matches.\n- AE reads the map layer's **source**: if the map has effects, it must be a\n  precomp.\n- **Falls back to shader** for midlevel ≠ 0.5, rotate, and mirror edges.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/edge-detect": {"title":"Edge Detect → shader","type":"edge-detect","class":"shader","body":"- Not Find Edges: AE's Find Edges is not a Sobel / Prewitt magnitude.\n  - Measured on noise: mean 0.063 with Invert on, 0.79 without.\n  - A hard-edged disc looks close, but only because it is mostly flat.\n- Exports as a Toolbox Shader region (9-tap gather).\n"},
  "ae-nodes/gaussian-blur": {"title":"Gaussian Blur (legacy) → Gaussian Blur","type":"gaussian-blur","class":"effect","body":"- The same map as `blur`: Blurriness = 1.7464 · radius.\n- Legacy saves load with `linearize: off`, which Gaussian Blur 2 cannot do,\n  so most legacy nodes fall back to shader.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/glsl-expression": {"title":"GLSL Expression → Toolbox Shader effect","type":"glsl-expression","class":"shader","body":"- A fused GLSL Expression becomes a Toolbox Shader effect on a comp-sized\n  solid or adjustment layer, with its bundle in `shaders/<id>.tbxfx`.\n- Image inputs `u_a`..`u_d` become the effect's Layer A–D params, pointing\n  at the layers or precomps that render the region's inputs.\n- Channels become the plug-in's sliders / colors / checkboxes; `pick()`\n  enums are baked to their current option; ramp / curve channels become\n  LUTs (static only).\n- Run `validate_ae_shader` on the node before exporting: it translates the\n  GLSL to Metal and compiles it the way the plug-in will (see `ae-host`\n  for what it refuses).\n- Export it through `export_ae_package({ fused: { \"<region target>\":\n  \"<this node's id>\" } })`; without that entry the region bakes.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/grain": {"title":"Grain → Add Grain (statistics match)","type":"grain","class":"effect","body":"- Maps to **Add Grain** (`VISINF Grain Implant`).\n  - Fixed: Viewing Mode Final Output, Blending Mode 5 (toolbox's overlay\n    response), Monochromatic, Size 1, Softness 0.\n  - Intensity = 8.67 · luminance. Random Seed = seed. Animation Speed 1, or\n    0 for static grain.\n- Grain is noise, so the match is statistical: the std of (out − in) per\n  luminance band is within 4% of toolbox's, and both are white at 1 px. The\n  random field itself differs.\n- Only the default look maps: custom preset, `fine` model, 1-px cells,\n  overlay at full mix, no chroma / tint / response / smoothing / drift, and\n  project-rate or static motion. Anything else → shader.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/keyer": {"title":"Keyer (color) → Linear Color Key","type":"keyer","class":"effect","body":"- `color` mode maps to **Linear Color Key** (`ADBE Linear Color Key2`),\n  Match Colors Using RGB, Key Colors.\n  - Key Color = key_color.\n  - Matching Tolerance = 100 · tolerance.\n  - Matching Softness = 150 · ((tol + soft)² − tol²).\n- AE keys on toolbox's own distance (|ΔRGB| / √3). Its matte is linear in d²\n  from tol², (d² − tol²) / (softness% / 150), where toolbox smoothsteps in d.\n  The softness above makes both reach 1 at tol + soft.\n- Measured on a colour sweep: α mean ≤ 0.027 (the largest softness is\n  worst), exact for a hard key.\n- **Falls back to shader** for:\n  - `chroma` (AE's chroma metric isn't toolbox's CbCr distance);\n  - `luma` (Extract measured off, α 0.035);\n  - `sample` mode;\n  - spill > 0.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/lut": {"title":"LUT → bake","type":"lut","class":"bake","body":"- **Apply Color LUT cannot be built by a script.**\n  - Adding the effect opens a file dialog: measured headless, the dialog\n    hangs aerender's render core.\n  - Its LUT file is not a scriptable property.\n- The GLSL table classes `lut` as opaque (the .cube lives in a param), so it\n  is not a shader region either: the node's output bakes.\n- Hand-off option for a designer: apply the same .cube in AE by hand.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/merge": {"title":"Merge → precomp layers, blend modes, track mattes","type":"merge","class":"layer","body":"- Each Merge input becomes a layer in a precomp, stacked in Merge's order,\n  with its blend mode and opacity (`layer_opacity:<id>` keys carry over).\n- A per-layer `mask:<id>` becomes a track matte by reference: Luma when\n  the mask is an image (luma × alpha), Alpha when it's a spline.\n  `maskInvert` makes it the Inverted type. The matte source layer is\n  hidden, as AE does for mattes.\n- 24 of the 29 blend modes map by name. Average, Negation, Reflect, Glow\n  and Phoenix have no AE mode: that Merge becomes a shader region (or a\n  bake without the plug-in).\n- Toolbox composites straight alpha, AE premultiplied: fills and mattes\n  match, anti-aliased edges of blended layers can differ sub-pixel.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/mirror": {"title":"Mirror → Mirror (bisect)","type":"mirror","class":"effect","body":"- `bisect` maps to **Mirror** (`ADBE Mirror`).\n  - Reflection Center is the line's point in px.\n  - Reflection Angle depends on the kept side: −x 0°, −y 90°, x 180°,\n    y 270°.\n- Measured: mean ≤ 0.006, worst 0.07 (resampling along the line).\n- **Falls back to shader** for:\n  - `x` / `y` / `both` / `radial`, which composite reflected copies over the\n    source (an opaque frame becomes its mirror image);\n  - Keep source off.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/pixelate": {"title":"Pixelate → Mosaic","type":"pixelate","class":"effect","body":"- Maps to **Mosaic** (`ADBE Mosaic`), Sharp Colors off.\n  - Horizontal Blocks = W / (size · aspect).\n  - Vertical Blocks = H / size.\n- Approximate: AE averages each block, while toolbox samples the cell centre.\n  - Measured on noise: mean 0.022 at size 16, 0.035 at size 32.\n  - Colour sweep at size 8: mean 0.0007.\n  - Sharp Colors on picks each block's bottom-right pixel, which is further\n    from toolbox's centre sample.\n- **Falls back to shader** when:\n  - the cells don't divide the comp (toolbox's grid starts bottom-left with\n    partial cells, Mosaic spreads whole blocks over the layer);\n  - the cells are circles.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/polar-coords": {"title":"Polar Coordinates → shader","type":"polar-coords","class":"shader","body":"- Not exported through AE's Polar Coordinates, whose conventions are fixed:\n  - the source's top row maps to the centre;\n  - angle 0 is at 12 o'clock;\n  - the source height spans the inscribed circle;\n  - everything outside that circle is transparent.\n- Toolbox's defaults differ on every one of those: the bottom row at the\n  centre, angle 0 at 3 o'clock, radius scale 1, clamped edges.\n  - The best toolbox settings still measure mean 0.19 (rect → polar) and\n    0.28 (polar → rect).\n  - Matching would need a flip, a scale and a wrap-around offset in front.\n- Exports as a Toolbox Shader region (the node is `pure` in the GLSL table).\n"},
  "ae-nodes/posterize": {"title":"Posterize → Levels + Posterize (exact)","type":"posterize","class":"effect","body":"- Two effects: **Levels** (`ADBE Easy Levels2`) with output range\n  [0.5/L, (L − 0.5)/L], then **Posterize** with Level = L.\n- Why the Levels: AE's Posterize bins at floor(v · L) / (L − 1), while\n  toolbox rounds to round(v · (L − 1)) / (L − 1). The Levels makes AE's floor\n  land on toolbox's rounding.\n- Exact on a ramp and on noise, L 2–32: max 0.0004 at 16 bpc, 0.002 at 8 bpc.\n- **Falls back to shader** for gamma ≠ 1 and for luma mode.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/sharpen": {"title":"Sharpen → Sharpen / Unsharp Mask","type":"sharpen","class":"effect","body":"- `box` maps to **Sharpen**, Sharpen Amount = 50 · amount.\n  - Matches away from the frame edge: mean 0.003, worst 0.023 with a 2-px\n    border excluded.\n  - The outermost pixels differ (worst 0.62), as AE pads differently.\n- `unsharp` maps to **Unsharp Mask**: Radius 0.5, Threshold 0,\n  Amount = 100 · amount.\n  - Exact: worst 0.0009 at 16 bpc, 0.007 at 8.\n  - Toolbox's unsharp is original + amount · (original − binomial 3×3).\n- **Falls back to shader** for `diamond` and `cross`, whose kernels Sharpen\n  doesn't have.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/stagger": {"title":"Stagger → per-copy keys","type":"stagger","class":"instances","body":"- Stagger writes a per-point `phase` channel. It has no AE object of its\n  own: what it drives is exported.\n- Phases that drive Copy to Points copies (through Modulate Points' scale /\n  rotate attributes, Map Attribute, a pick, tint or opacity) are evaluated\n  at every frame of the layer's window. Each exploded copy gets keys only\n  where its motion bends: linear stretches merge, so a hold → ramp → hold\n  copy has about 3 keys. Exact at frames.\n- A pick driven by a phase (attribute pick) becomes one layer per variant,\n  switched by HOLD opacity keys.\n- Phases that drive geometry directly (a spline built from the points)\n  become path keys per frame. That needs a constant vertex count.\n- The Stagger node is pure, so a Time Offset or a clip window retimes it\n  exactly; the keys land on the comp clock.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/text": {"title":"Text → AE text layer","type":"text","class":"text","body":"- Approximate. Font (PostScript name), size, tracking, leading, case,\n  alignment and box map to a TextDocument; px at the working resolution\n  are AE px.\n- The AE machine needs the fonts installed; the report lists them.\n- New text layers inherit AE's Character panel settings, so every\n  attribute is set explicitly by the builder.\n- Bakes for now: animators, text on a path, a keyed text document\n  (content, font, size…) and gradient or image fills. AE animators with\n  Range Selectors and Path Options are the next wave.\n- Variable-font axes: AE sets them only inside text animators, so the\n  named instance is used (approx).\n- Glyph metrics differ between toolbox's rasterizer and AE; offer outlines\n  when the layout must match exactly.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/threshold": {"title":"Threshold → Channel Mixer + Threshold","type":"threshold","class":"effect","body":"- Two effects: **Channel Mixer**, monochrome with Rec.709 weights (21.26 /\n  71.52 / 7.22), then **Threshold** (`ADBE Threshold2`) with Level =\n  threshold (0–1, not 0–255).\n- Why the Channel Mixer: AE's Threshold reads Rec.601 luma, toolbox's\n  Rec.709. On saturated colours that flips up to 7% of pixels; the mixer\n  hands Threshold 709 grey.\n- Exact except pixels lying on the threshold itself: ≤ 0.5% of\n  pixels.\n- **Falls back to shader** for softness > 0 and for invert.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/trails": {"title":"Trails (feedback) → Echo","type":"trails","class":"effect","body":"- `feedback` maps to **Echo** (`ADBE Echo`).\n  - Echo Time = −1/fps, Decay = decay, Starting Intensity 1.\n  - Operator: Composite In Back (the current frame over its echoes).\n  - Echoes until decay^n < 0.5/255: n = ⌈ln(0.5/255) / ln decay⌉, at most\n    255 (75 at decay 0.92).\n- Measured on a disc moving over 16 frames (decay 0.5 / 0.8 / 0.92): colours\n  exact at 16 bpc, alpha mean ≤ 0.019.\n- Echo reads the layer's **source** frames and ignores effects before it:\n  the trails input must be a precomp.\n- Toolbox's trail depends on evaluating every frame in order; the offline\n  export does.\n- `ring` (a stop-motion hold) and `velocity` modes have no Echo form: bake.\n"},
  "ae-nodes/transform": {"title":"Transform → AE layer transform","type":"transform","class":"transform","body":"- Exact. `anchorPoint = pivot_px`, `position = pivot_px + translate_px`,\n  `scale ·100 %`, `rotation` in degrees (clockwise on screen).\n- On a shape chain it becomes the shape group's transform; ending a layer\n  it becomes the layer's own transform; mid-chain on an image it also\n  becomes a layer transform, on a precomp when the layer's own transform\n  is already taken.\n- Bakes for now: `tile` (Motion Tile), `legacySkew`, and an image\n  Transform driven by a wired transform.\n- `space=local` pivots come from the incoming geometry's bounding box. If\n  the box animates, the anchor is keyed per frame and the report says so.\n- Independent translate X / Y tracks export as separated dimensions, each\n  with its own keys and eases.\n- Scale is clamped ≥ 0.0001 in toolbox, so a \"negative scale\" flip is a\n  rotation plus mirror, not a negative AE scale.\n"},
};
